to a Likely R race, but the newest polls split between a 10-point Scott lead and a 6-point Janoo lead, suggesting genuine tightening. Averaging the conflicting surveys and markets yields a modest Scott edge of roughly six points.", "watch": "Whether the UNH survey reflects a real shift toward Janoo or an outlier; another round of polling would clarify.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Phil Scott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Vermont Governor Phil Scott, a Republican in one of the nation's most Democratic-leaning states, seeks another term against Democrat Amanda Janoo. Scott has historically won by wide margins thanks to a cross-partisan personal brand, and most expert raters still call the race Solid or Likely R. Prediction markets give him roughly an 82% chance of winning.\n\nThe race has tightened, though. A late-September Vermont Public poll shows Scott ahead by 10 points, but a University of New Hampshire survey from the same period puts Janoo up 6, the closest contest in a decade. The conflicting polls and Scott's incumbency edge point to a modest but real Republican advantage, with meaningful uncertainty about whether the recent shift toward Janoo is durable.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2101, "margin": -4.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -10.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2344, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2363, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2631, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2569, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1727, "margin": -6.0}]}